    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0421" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.125/78: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sheffield</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-04T11:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>327. Department’s 244, July 24, noon. Representative of Foreign Office at
                    conference will be Antonio Castro Leal, Counselor of Mexican Embassy at
                        Washington.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d247-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheffield</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d247-f1" n="27" xml:id="d247-f1-content">
                <p>The American representatives were Dr. John R. Mohler, Chief of the Bureau of
                    Animal Industry; Dr. Arthur W. Miller, Chief of the Field Inspection Division of
                    that Bureau; and Mr. Richard W. Flournoy, Jr., Assistant to the Solicitor of the
                    Department of State (file No. 611.125/73).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
